+### §viewport-not-container — the shell's layout step follows the viewport width
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: the shell's layout step is a viewport `@media (min-width: 720px)` query. `.shell` is no longer a size
+  container (`container-type` removed).
+- Reason: the maintainer explicitly overrode §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15) on 2026-10-23.
+- Known cost: the override brings back the 2026-09-14 behavior. In a split pane narrower than 720px on a wide screen,
+  the shell takes the two-column layout and the 240px sidebar can be clipped.
+- Replaces: §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15), which required `@container` queries on `.shell` and forbade viewport
+  `@media` width queries because of that incident.
